The bug was an off-by-one error in src/parse.py:4. The function was using `parts[1]` to return the first word, but it should have been `parts[0]` since Python lists are 0-indexed. This caused:
- `test_basic` to fail because it returned 'world' instead of 'hello'
- `test_single` to error because there's no index 1 when the string has only one word

The fix was simple: change `return parts[1]` to `return parts[0]`.
